nge log in a few sections:\n Guidelines:\n \n - All bullet point in the summary should be concise and rarely exceed a single line of 120 characters (excluding PR links)\n+- Do not wrap or break lines within a bullet point or paragraph - each bullet point must fit on a single line (PR links allowed to exceed the line limit)\n - Avoid repeating `ggml`-specific changes - these should already be covered by the `ggml` release links\n - Provide PR link for each bullet point where possible\n - Don't add bullet point to state that there are no API changes in some module\n-- Combine related topics (a full list of commits will be appended independently at end of the summary)\n+- Group similar/related items into a single bullet with multiple trailing PR links, one bullet per topic\n+  - A full list of commits will be appended independently at end of the summary, so it is not a problem to skip some less important changes\n - Skip minor-impact notes (e.g. \"fix compile warnings\", \"refactored code\", ...)\n \n Output just the summary in a markdown block, without any extra text. Save it to a local text file called `release-notes-vX.Y.Z.txt`."}]}